# A REQUIRED ARGUMENT IS REQUIRED WHATEVER DECLARES IT. A generic function and
# a native one are held to the rule a plain function always was: only a
# parameter carrying a DEFAULT may be left out at the call site.
#
# All three lines were accepted in silence. The native method call was the worst
# of them -- `insert` short of `at:` emitted `z_t475_insert(&z_v1, 1, 0)` and
# RAN, the missing argument quietly zero.
main: function is {
    print
    ns: (ListVal i64)
    ns.append from: 1
    (ns.insert from: 2)
    io.writeText path: "/tmp/zprobe.txt"
}
